    <fr:route>/def-0007/</fr:route>
    <fr:title text="Monoid">Monoid</fr:title>
    <fr:taxon>Definition</fr:taxon>
  </fr:frontmatter>
  <fr:mainmatter>
    <html:p>
A set <fr:tex display="inline">S</fr:tex> equipped with a binary operation <fr:tex display="inline">S\times  S\to  S</fr:tex>, which we will denote <fr:tex display="inline">\circ </fr:tex>, is a <html:strong>monoid</html:strong> if it satisfies the following two axioms:
<html:ul><html:li>Associativity: <fr:tex display="inline">\forall  a,b,c\in  S, (a\circ  b) \circ  c= a \circ  (b \circ  c)</fr:tex></html:li>
<html:li>Identity: <fr:tex display="inline">\exists  e\in  S</fr:tex> such that <fr:tex display="inline">\forall  g\in  S, g\circ  e=e\circ  g = g</fr:tex></html:li></html:ul></html:p>
  </fr:mainmatter>
